course: dictionary
lesson: 14977
title: Renovate: making old things new
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Renovate is a verb, so it is an action word. To renovate something is to repair it and make it look new and in good condition again. «The family will renovate the old kitchen this summer.» They will fix it up so the kitchen looks new.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «The council renovated the park, and now the swings are bright and new.» The words bright and new tell you what happened: the park was made good again. Renovate is often used for buildings, but you can also renovate old furniture.
explain: Words change their endings. Renovate, renovates, renovated and renovating are all forms of the same word. «Sam renovated the wobbly chair with new paint and screws» tells us the work is already done, so renovated is the past tense.
fact: Renovate means to repair something and make it look new and in good condition again.
fact: «Renovate» can be used for buildings, like «renovate a house», and for old furniture.
fact: «Renovated» means already repaired and made new, as in «a newly renovated school».
fact: «Under renovation» means being repaired at the moment.
fact: Renovating things often costs money, so maths problems can ask you to work out the cost.
exercise: «The council will renovate the park.» What does renovate mean here? | *Repair it and make it look new again | Sell it quickly | Paint it black | Knock it down and leave it empty
exercise: «Sam renovated the old chair.» Which word is the past tense of renovate? | *renovated | renovates | renovating | renovation
exercise: «It costs £40 to renovate one chair.» How much would it cost to renovate 3 chairs? | £80 | *£120 | £37 | £43
test: «The school is under renovation, so we are using the hall for lessons.» What does under renovation mean? | Being painted red | *Being repaired and made new | Closed forever | Having a party
test: «The old barn was newly renovated and now it looks like new.» What does newly renovated mean? | *Repaired and made to look new | Very old and falling down | Moved to another town | Painted with stripes
exam: A team can renovate 2 rooms each day. How many rooms can they renovate in 5 days? | 3 | 25 | 7 | *10
